==Strategy==
While the Alien enemies are limited, the Cyberhorn's stats become massively inflated at higher magnifications, reaching 1,200,000 HP at max level. As such, it's not recommended to challenge this gauntlet until all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] are obtained.

This is one of the simpler Monthly Gauntlets, as there is a lack of strong peons; it helps that Heavenly Le'saint's Angel typing leaves him prone to being stalled out by [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]. Stall the initial Cyberhorn with anti-Alien crowd controllers (e.g. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]]), alongside your choice of [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] or Soap Cat. Once the base is hit, beat down Heavenly Le'saint with whatever anti-Angel cats you own. Letting him come to your base and defending with Ramen Cat while attacking with any cat outranging him (>320 range, e.g. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]) is a pretty good way to get around the Cat Limit.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - Basically mandatory for this stage, as he prevents Heavenly Le'saint from pushing very hard. It's not recommended to use him against the initial starting Cyberhorn, however, especially at higher magnifications.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] - With its high speed, it can rush into the frontlines and deal huge burst damage to either Heavenly Le'saint or an annoying Gabriel blocking the way.
*[[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] - Though a relatively late-game unit, Bubble Cat is able to comfortably outrange Heavenly Le'saint while chewing through its giant health pool with its Massive Damage vs. Angels.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Anti-Angel Nukers - Ubers such as [[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]], [[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Colossal Benkei]], [[Voluptuous Peony - Daji (Uber Rare Cat)|Voluptuous Peony - Daji]], [[Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sonic]] and more will help to massively reduce the amount of time it takes to kill Heavenly Le'saint.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]] - Being a unit that has knockback against Aliens and Angels, Thunder Jack can make this stage a joke by stunlocking Le'Saint.

